.TH CCOL_DYNMQ_RECV_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_dynmq_recv_zc \- receive a message from a dynamic queue (it blocks)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_dynmq_recv_zc(ccol_dynamic_queue *dq, c_message_t *target_buf);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function blocks until a message arrives in the dynamic queue, then
removes the message at the head and transfers the ownership of its data
pointer to the caller in target_buf. The caller must free
target_buf->data after it finishes with the data.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
dq          Dynamic queue to receive from
target_buf  Buffer that gets the message together with the ownership
            of the data.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        - The function received a message. The caller must
                      free target_buf->data.
ccol_invalid_args   - dq or target_buf is NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The function blocks with no time limit while it waits for a message.
The function stays blocked while sends on the queue are off, and it
  unblocks after a call turns sends on again and a message arrives.
The caller gets the ownership of target_buf->data and must free it.
The function is thread-safe.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_dynmq_try_recv_zc (3),
.BR ccol_dynmq_timed_recv_zc (3),
.BR ccol_dynmq_send_zc (3)
